{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>His daughters.</b> This is Dinah. And likewise (Genesis 46:23–24): ״ובני דן חושים״, (1 Chronicles 2:8): ״ובני איתן עזריהו״. From here our Rabbis of blessed memory learned: one who says, 'my property is for my sons,' and he had a son and a daughter — the son takes everything. And they raised an objection in the Gemara: who calls a man 'my sons'? He said to him: yes, as it is written (Numbers 26:8–9): ״ובני פלוא אליאב״. <b>And his granddaughters.</b> Serach the daughter of Asher."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:40.781484912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}